Each ported file carries the header "Derived from datatrove 0.10.1
(Apache-2.0), © HuggingFace; modified." datatrove's punctuation tables were
extracted from datatrove itself by crates/pyroid-core/src/filters/generate_tables.py.

The MinHash deduplication port (crates/pyroid-core/src/dedup/,
crates/pyroid-core/tests/dedup_data/, crates/pyroid-py/src/dedup.rs,
python/pyroid/dedup.py and python/pyroid/dedup.pyi) is a derivative work of
datatrove 0.10.1 (MinhashDedupSignature, MinhashDedupBuckets,
MinhashDedupCluster, MinhashDedupFilter and simplify_text), under the same
Apache-2.0 licence. Each ported file carries the header "Derived from
datatrove 0.10.1 (Apache-2.0), © HuggingFace Inc.; modified." The permutation
parameters reproduce numpy's legacy RandomState (MT19937 and masked bounded
integers; numpy is BSD-3-Clause); no numpy code is included.

The further datatrove steps (crates/pyroid-core/src/filters/pii.rs,
badwords.rs, url.rs, symbol_lines.rs, crates/pyroid-core/src/dedup/sentence.rs,
their sections of crates/pyroid-py/src/filters.rs and dedup.rs, of
python/pyroid/filters.py[i] and dedup.py[i], and
python/pyroid/integrations/datatrove.py) are derivative works of datatrove
0.10.1 (PIIFormatter, C4BadWordsFilter, URLFilter, SymbolLinesFormatter,
SentenceDedupSignature, SentenceFindDedups, SentenceDedupFilter and
SentenceDedupBuildIndex), under the same Apache-2.0 licence, with the same
file headers.

pyroid ships none of the word lists or blocklists these steps use: the LDNOOBW
"List of Dirty, Naughty, Obscene, and Otherwise Bad Words" (CC BY 4.0,
https://github.com/LDNOOBW/List-of-Dirty-Naughty-Obscene-and-Otherwise-Bad-Words)
is downloaded at run time from the commits datatrove pins, and URLFilter's
lists are read from the user or from an installed datatrove.

