NLTK tokenizers (pyroid.nltk)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The tokenizer port (crates/pyroid-core/src/nltk/, crates/pyroid-py/src/nltk.rs,
python/pyroid/nltk/ and its .pyi stub) is a derivative work of NLTK 3.10.4,
https://www.nltk.org (sdist sha256
44679f4e9220abfd496d2c8cdb22f8425ccbe557604f9aa5cacb1c44003dabc1): the Punkt
sentence tokenizer (nltk/tokenize/punkt.py, nltk/tabdata.py), the Treebank
tokenizers and detokenizer (nltk/tokenize/treebank.py, destructive.py,
util.py), sent_tokenize and word_tokenize (nltk/tokenize/__init__.py) and the
model search path (nltk/data.py):

    Copyright (C) 2001-2026 NLTK Project

    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt).

Each ported file carries the header "Derived from NLTK 3.10.4 (Apache-2.0),
© 2001-2026 NLTK Project; modified." The Punkt algorithm is Kiss, Tibor and
Strunk, Jan (2006): Unsupervised Multilingual Sentence Boundary Detection.
Computational Linguistics 32: 485-525. The Treebank rules follow Robert
MacIntyre's tokenizer.sed for the Penn Treebank.

crates/pyroid-core/src/nltk/tables.rs is generated by generate_tables.py from
the character classes of the regex module 2026.9.29 (Apache-2.0 / CNRI-Python;
its Unicode Character Database data is under the Unicode License v3) and from
CPython's str methods; it holds code point ranges only.

The pretrained Punkt models (nltk_data's punkt_tab) are not included: their
licence is unstated (nltk_data's DATASET-LICENSES.md lists them as having no
licence attribute). pyroid reads the copy the user installs. The test
recordings under crates/pyroid-core/src/nltk/testdata/ are outputs of NLTK on
public text (FineWeb, ODC-By 1.0) and on parameters NLTK's PunktTrainer learned
from that text; they contain no part of the punkt_tab models.

