SudachiPy / sudachi.rs (the Japanese word tokenizer)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
crates/pyroid-core/src/sudachi/ (except ja.rs and replay.rs) is a
derivative work of SudachiPy 0.7.0, https://github.com/WorksApplications/sudachi.rs
(© 2021-2026 Works Applications Co., Ltd., Apache License 2.0, a copy of which
is in LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt): the dictionary reader, the input-text, OOV and
path-rewrite plugins of its default configuration, the lattice and the A-unit
split of sudachi.rs were rewritten in Rust. Each ported file carries the header
"Derived from sudachi.rs 0.7.0 (Apache-2.0), © Works Applications Co., Ltd.;
modified."

crates/pyroid-core/src/sudachi/resources/char.def, unk.def and rewrite.def are
copied unmodified from the same release (PyPI sdist sudachipy-0.7.0.tar.gz,
sha256 14a2505e7d086fe9da64c0048d8e2de13cdded3aac4f1e047929cef51dba338c,
resources/), under the same licence.

pyroid does not ship a Sudachi dictionary. It reads the SudachiDict system
dictionary the user installs (sudachidict-core, Apache License 2.0,
https://github.com/WorksApplications/SudachiDict). The test recordings in
crates/pyroid-core/src/sudachi/testdata/ hold SudachiPy's output with
sudachidict-core 20261015 (word and POS ids), and tags.json its POS table (1,558
part-of-speech names); no lexicon, connection matrix or other dictionary file
is included.

crates/pyroid-core/src/sudachi/ja.rs also follows datatrove 0.10.1's
SpaCyTokenizer and datatrove.utils.japanese_tokenizer (Apache-2.0) and spaCy
3.8.18's Japanese tokenizer and sentencizer (MIT), both described above.

